{"black_box_warning":{"current_value":"Current row boxed-warning text uses the Ativan Injection wording for lorazepam injection.","fda_source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/fda-requiring-boxed-warning-updated-improve-safe-use-benzodiazepine-drug-class"],"proposed_value":"No change to fda_black_box_warning text. Replace the source with an FDA/Drugs@FDA label source; do not use DailyMed for this field.","rationale":"The warning text is supported by the FDA Ativan Injection label. The current fda_black_box_warning_source cites DailyMed, which violates the row policy even though the warning itself is FDA-label-consistent.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified"},"blocking_questions":[],"fact_checks":[{"current_value":"lorazepam","field":"generic_name","proposed_value":"lorazepam","rationale":"FDA labels and PubMed RCT records identify the active ingredient as lorazepam.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/017794s049lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"","field":"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"","rationale":"No separate alternate generic name requiring a separate row was identified; Ativan and Loreev XR are trade names for lorazepam.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/017794s049lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/nda/2022/214826Orig1s000Approv.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Ativan; Loreev XR","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Ativan; Loreev XR","rationale":"Ativan and Loreev XR are FDA-supported lorazepam brand names. The deterministic suggestion to replace trade_names with 'Lorazepam' is not correct because lorazepam is the generic name, not a trade name.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/017794s049lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/nda/2022/214826Orig1s000Approv.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Yes","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"Yes","rationale":"FDA labeling/approval records support U.S. availability of lorazepam products including Ativan, lorazepam oral concentrate, injection, and Loreev XR.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/017794s049lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2009/079244lbl.PDF","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/nda/2022/214826Orig1s000Approv.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Tablet; oral concentrate; IV/IM injection","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Tablet; oral concentrate; IV/IM injection; extended-release capsule","rationale":"The current value is incomplete because FDA approved Loreev XR lorazepam extended-release capsules. Tablet, oral concentrate, and IV/IM injection are supported by FDA labels.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/017794s049lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2009/079244lbl.PDF","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/214826s003lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"CNS: sedation 16%, CNS: dizziness 7%, constitutional: weakness 4%, respiratory: respiratory depression 3%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"CNS: sedation 15.9%, CNS: dizziness 6.9%, constitutional: weakness 4.2%, CNS: unsteadiness 3.4%","rationale":"FDA tablet/oral concentrate labeling gives sedation 15.9%, dizziness 6.9%, weakness 4.2%, and unsteadiness 3.4%. Respiratory depression is listed as an adverse reaction/warning but not as a 3% event in the cited labeling.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/017794s049lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2009/079244lbl.PDF"]},{"current_value":"Status epilepticus; Seizure clusters / rescue","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Status epilepticus; Seizure clusters / rescue","rationale":"FDA injection labeling supports status epilepticus. The seizure-clusters/rescue portion is plausible clinically but needs a named trusted source in the row; the cited FDA label does not specifically support seizure clusters.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Not a CYP inducer/inhibitor; glucuronidated","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Not a CYP inducer/inhibitor; glucuronidated","rationale":"FDA labeling supports hepatic glucuronidation, inactive lorazepam glucuronide, and that cytochrome oxidation is not involved. The CYP inducer/inhibitor wording is a reasonable summary of that label information.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/017794s049lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"10-20 h","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"10-20 h","rationale":"FDA injection labeling reports terminal half-life 14 +/- 5 hours; oral concentrate labeling reports about 12 hours for unconjugated lorazepam.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2009/079244lbl.PDF"]},{"current_value":"Liver","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Liver","rationale":"FDA labeling states lorazepam is extensively conjugated to lorazepam glucuronide in the liver; the inactive metabolite is eliminated mainly by kidneys.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Acute seizure dosing individualized","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"Status epilepticus: 4 mg IV slowly; may repeat 4 mg IV once after 10-15 minutes if seizures continue or recur; experience with further doses is very limited. Oral anxiety labeling: 1-10 mg/day.","rationale":"The current text is too vague for a maximum-dose field. FDA labeling gives the adult status epilepticus regimen and oral daily dosage range.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/017794s049lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Acute seizure/status dosing individualized","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"No chronic epilepsy minimum effective dose; status epilepticus adult FDA-labeled regimen is 4 mg IV slowly, with one repeat 4 mg dose after 10-15 minutes if needed.","rationale":"The row's value is directionally correct that this is acute/intermittent treatment, but FDA labeling supports a more precise status epilepticus regimen.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Benzodiazepine positive allosteric modulator of GABA-A receptors; enhances GABAergic inhibition and is used acutely for seizure termination.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"Benzodiazepine positive allosteric modulator of GABA-A receptors; enhances GABAergic inhibition and is used acutely for seizure termination.","rationale":"FDA injection labeling states lorazepam interacts with the GABA-benzodiazepine receptor complex, enhances GABA affinity for its receptor site, and reduces seizure activity.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No clinically meaningful QT effect established","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"No clinically meaningful QT effect established","rationale":"No contradiction was found in the reviewed FDA labels, but the row lacks a named source specifically supporting the QT statement.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":[]},{"current_value":"1977","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"1977","rationale":"FDA review material for Loreev XR states lorazepam was first approved as Ativan tablets in 1977; current value is acceptable as a year-only field.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/nda/2022/214826Orig1s000MultidisciplineR.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Wikipedia anticonvulsant drug-class list; American Epilepsy Society 2024 U.S. ASM summary; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/Drugs@FDA labeling (Ativan tablets NDA 017794; Ativan injection NDA 018140; Loreev XR NDA 214826; lorazepam oral concentrate ANDA 079244); PubMed/NCBI RCT records; ClinicalTrials.gov NCT00004297","rationale":"Wikipedia is not in the trusted source list, and DailyMed must not be used for FDA boxed-warning verification. The proposed source text names trusted FDA, PubMed/NCBI, and ClinicalTrials.gov sources actually used for the checked facts.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/017794s049lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6378615/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11547716/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00004297"]}],"generic_name":"lorazepam","missing_rcts":[{"pmid":"11547716","proposed_link_text":"Alldredge2001|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11547716/","title":"A comparison of lorazepam, diazepam, and placebo for the treatment of out-of-hospital status epilepticus","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11547716/","why_relevant":"PubMed verifies a randomized double-blind trial of IV lorazepam, diazepam, and placebo for out-of-hospital status epilepticus; ClinicalTrials.gov NCT00004297 identifies the study as phase III. Lorazepam 59.1% vs placebo 21.1% termination of status epilepticus on ED arrival is extractable as an acute seizure-termination endpoint, not RR50/MPC."}],"outcome_checks":[{"current_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo RR50 differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","field":"diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo RR50 differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","rationale":"Walker1984 and Alldredge2001 do not report a chronic epilepsy >=50% seizure-frequency responder endpoint suitable for this field.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6378615/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11547716/"]},{"current_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo MPC differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo MPC differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","rationale":"No cited or newly identified lorazepam placebo-controlled phase II/III record reports a median percent seizure-frequency change endpoint suitable for this field.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6378615/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11547716/"]},{"current_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","rationale":"Alldredge2001 reports acute termination of status epilepticus on ED arrival, not a standard seizure-freedom patient-rate endpoint. If the CSV intentionally maps acute termination to this field, the extractable differential would be +38.0 percentage points (59.1% lorazepam minus 21.1% placebo), but that mapping needs user approval.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11547716/"]}],"overall_status":"needs_update","proposed_row_updates":[{"current_value":"CNS: sedation 16%, CNS: dizziness 7%, constitutional: weakness 4%, respiratory: respiratory depression 3%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"CNS: sedation 15.9%, CNS: dizziness 6.9%, constitutional: weakness 4.2%, CNS: unsteadiness 3.4%","reason":"Corrects the FDA-labeled common adverse event percentages and replaces unsupported respiratory depression 3%.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/017794s049lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Tablet; oral concentrate; IV/IM injection","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Tablet; oral concentrate; IV/IM injection; extended-release capsule","reason":"Adds FDA-approved Loreev XR extended-release capsule formulation.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/214826s003lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/nda/2022/214826Orig1s000Approv.pdf"]},{"current_value":"IV/IM injection; Liquid; Tablet","field":"filter_formulation","proposed_value":"Capsule; IV/IM injection; Liquid; Tablet","reason":"Derived filter should include the FDA-approved Loreev XR extended-release capsule formulation.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/214826s003lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Acute seizure dosing individualized","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"Status epilepticus: 4 mg IV slowly; may repeat 4 mg IV once after 10-15 minutes if seizures continue or recur; experience with further doses is very limited. Oral anxiety labeling: 1-10 mg/day.","reason":"FDA labels provide more precise acute status epilepticus and oral dosing limits than the current vague wording.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/017794s049lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Acute seizure/status dosing individualized","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"No chronic epilepsy minimum effective dose; status epilepticus adult FDA-labeled regimen is 4 mg IV slowly, with one repeat 4 mg dose after 10-15 minutes if needed.","reason":"Clarifies that lorazepam does not have a chronic epilepsy minimum effective dose and cites the FDA status epilepticus regimen.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Walker1984|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6378615/","field":"pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","proposed_value":"Alldredge2001|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11547716/","reason":"Walker1984 is placebo-controlled and randomized but not verified as phase II/III. Alldredge2001 is the missing placebo-controlled lorazepam status epilepticus RCT associated with phase III NCT00004297.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6378615/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11547716/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00004297"]},{"current_value":"PubMed loop 29/65 on 2026-05-15: 1 qualifying placebo-controlled randomized clinical trial report(s) retained from 11 PubMed candidate(s). Links were rebuilt from fetched PubMed PMID metadata and named FirstAuthorYear. Differential effectiveness columns summarize extractable maximum effective dose/regimen values within qualifying RCT reports.","field":"rct_pubmed_verification_notes","proposed_value":"Audit 2026-05-21: Walker1984 PMID 6378615 is a lorazepam double-blind placebo-controlled crossover clinical trial but is not verified as phase II/III. Alldredge2001 PMID 11547716 is a randomized double-blind lorazepam/diazepam/placebo out-of-hospital status epilepticus trial associated with phase III NCT00004297 and should be included if this field is restricted to phase II/III placebo-controlled RCTs. RR50, MPC, and standard seizure-freedom endpoints remain not extractable; Alldredge2001 reports acute status-termination 59.1% lorazepam vs 21.1% placebo.","reason":"Corrects the retained/rejected RCT interpretation and documents the extractable acute endpoint separately from RR50/MPC/seizure freedom.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6378615/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11547716/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00004297"]},{"current_value":"AES/FDA summary","field":"mechanism_source_tier","proposed_value":"FDA labeling","reason":"The reviewed trusted source directly supporting the mechanism is FDA labeling; AES was not cited from a trusted source URL in this audit bundle.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"Walker1984","pmid":"6378615","proposed_action":"Do not count as a phase II/III RCT unless the dataset permits historical non-phase placebo-controlled trials; otherwise replace with Alldredge2001 for the phase II/III field.","rationale":"PubMed verifies lorazepam, randomized assignment, double-blind placebo-controlled crossover design, and PMID 6378615. PubMed publication type is Clinical Trial, not Phase II/III, and the trial had only eight patients.","status":"not_phase_ii_iii","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6378615/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=boxed_warning_found; setid=5fc0e987-61c9-40c4-b0d5-fcea07c8733e; published=Apr 10, 2023; title=ATIVAN (LORAZEPAM) INJECTION [HIKMA PHARMACEUTICALS USA INC.]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=5fc0e987-61c9-40c4-b0d5-fcea07c8733e","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/Drugs@FDA label; status=boxed_warning_found; NDA=018140; Reference ID=5109772; title=ATIVAN Injection (lorazepam injection, USP); revised=Jan 2023; url=https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf","reason":"DailyMed is not permissible for the FDA black-box-warning field; the FDA accessdata label supports the current warning text.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"05-20-2026","field":"fda_black_box_warning_verified","proposed_value":"05-21-2026","reason":"Boxed warning was rechecked against an FDA label source during this audit.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Wikipedia anticonvulsant drug-class list; American Epilepsy Society 2024 U.S. ASM summary; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/Drugs@FDA labeling (Ativan tablets NDA 017794; Ativan injection NDA 018140; Loreev XR NDA 214826; lorazepam oral concentrate ANDA 079244); PubMed/NCBI RCT records; ClinicalTrials.gov NCT00004297","reason":"Replaces non-trusted/impermissible source names with trusted source categories that support the checked cells.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/017794s049lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2009/079244lbl.PDF","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/214826s003lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11547716/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00004297"]},{"current_value":"American Epilepsy Society 2024 U.S. ASM summary; Sills and Rogawski 2020 ASM mechanism review","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA Ativan Injection label","reason":"FDA labeling directly supports the GABA-benzodiazepine receptor mechanism used in the row; AES was not verified from a trusted URL in this audit.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/018140s051lbl.pdf"]}],"summary":"Lorazepam row needs updates. The FDA boxed warning text is supportable from an FDA label, but the source field must stop citing DailyMed. Main data issues: common adverse percentages contain an unsupported respiratory-depression 3% entry, formulations omit Loreev XR extended-release capsules, the phase II/III PubMed RCT field incorrectly relies on Walker1984 and misses Alldredge2001, and several source fields cite non-trusted or non-specific sources."}
